# Ruijie RGOS show interface transceiver parser with DDM fields.
#
# Sample input (templates/samples/ruijie_10_62_63_21_show_interfaces_transceiver.txt):
#   ========Interface TenGigabitEthernet 1/47========
#   Transceiver Type    :  10GBASE-SR-SFP+
#   ...
#   Vendor Serial Number           : G1PT549427799
#
#   Current diagnostic parameters[AP:Average Power]:
#   Temp(Celsius)   Voltage(V)      Bias(mA)            RX power(dBm)       TX power(dBm)
#   39(OK)          3.27(OK)        6.68(OK)            -2.99(OK)[AP]       -2.40(OK)
#
# Field semantics:
#   INTERFACE — device interface name (TenGigabitEthernet 1/47).
#   SN        — vendor serial number (Vendor Serial Number).
#   BIAS      — DDM bias current in milliamps (DDM row, Bias column value
#               before the "(OK)" suffix).
#   TX_POWER  — DDM transmit power in dBm.
#   RX_POWER  — DDM receive power in dBm.
#
# WARNING 4 mitigation: this template is referenced by
# RuijieCliCollector.ParseTransceiverDDM — no dead TextFSM templates in
# the project.
#
# D-10 (RESEARCH Pitfall 5): the Wave 2 collector filters transceiver
# rows by the up-interface list produced by show interfaces status
# BEFORE parsing this template. The Go collector applies the up-filter
# post-parse.

Value Required INTERFACE (\S+(?:\s+\S+)*?)
Value SN (\S+)
Value BIAS (\S+?)
Value TX_POWER (\S+?)
Value RX_POWER (\S+?)

Start
  ^========Interface\s+${INTERFACE}========
  ^Vendor\s+Serial\s+Number\s*:\s*${SN}\s*$$
  ^\d+\(OK\)\s+\d+\.\d+\(OK\)\s+${BIAS}\(OK\)\s+${RX_POWER}\(OK\).+${TX_POWER}\(OK\)\s*$$ -> Record
  ^\d+\(OK\)\s+\d+\.\d+\(OK\)\s+${BIAS}\(OK\)\s+${RX_POWER}\(OK\).+\S+\(OK\)\s*$$ -> Record
